# After a redef, a child of a production it keeps with [...] is read by its
# label from outside the parse, and a child of a production it adds by its
# type's name. colm refused S.Name: the redef's object had no names for the
# kept productions' children.

lex
	literal `;
	token id /[a-z]+/
	token number /[0-9]+/
	ignore /space+/
end

def statement
	[Name: id `;]

redef statement
	[number `;]
|	[...]

parse S: statement[ "x;" ]
print( $S.Name, "\n" )
parse T: statement[ "7;" ]
print( $T.number, "\n" )
##### EXP #####
x
7
